{% comment %}
  Messages used to be stored HTML-escaped (raw_escape_string in
  channels/conversate/receive), so every consumer that didn't render them as HTML -
  the JSON API, push notifications, the sidebar preview - showed &lt; &amp; etc.
  literally. They're now stored as typed and escaped at render time; this turns the
  existing ones back into the typed text.

  Reverses exactly what raw_escape_string produces (&lt; &gt; &quot; &#39; &amp;),
  &amp; last so an escaped "&amp;lt;" (typed "&lt;") comes back as "&lt;", not "<".

  One background job per page of messages, so a big table doesn't time out the
  deploy. Pages are taken over the whole table sorted by id - not filtered by
  content - so updating a message doesn't shift the pages other jobs work on.
{% endcomment %}
{% liquid
  assign per_page = 100
  graphql r = 'modules/chat/messages/search_for_unescape', page: 1, limit: per_page
  assign total_pages = r.messages.total_pages

  for page in (1..total_pages)
    background _job = 'modules/chat/migrations/unescape_messages_page', page: page, per_page: per_page
  endfor

  log total_pages, type: 'chat: unescape stored messages - pages scheduled'
%}
